IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `tas-provisions`

-- Acts Interpretation Act 1931 (Tasmania): the cross-references, as data.
-- Every reference in the deposited text from one provision to another provision of the same text is an `Internal cross-reference` row:
-- the citing provision, the words of the citation as printed, the identifier it cites and the heading of the cited provision as the text prints it ("" where it prints none).
-- A reference to another Act or instrument is an `External cross-reference` row: the instrument and the provision as printed. It is not resolved here.
-- A script finds the references by pattern over the text file and resolves each against the provision index; it is not a reading of the text by a person.

DECLARE `Internal cross-reference` HAS
    `citing provision`           IS A STRING
    `words as printed`           IS A STRING
    `cited provision`            IS A STRING
    `heading of cited provision` IS A STRING

DECLARE `External cross-reference` HAS
    `citing provision`      IS A STRING
    `words as printed`      IS A STRING
    `instrument as printed` IS A STRING
    `provision as printed`  IS A STRING

`the internal cross-references` MEANS LIST
