GIVEN r IS AN `Internal cross-reference`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the internal cross-reference resolves` r MEANS
        `the provision is indexed` (r's `citing provision`)
    AND CONSIDER `the heading as printed of provision` (r's `cited provision`)
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
        WHEN JUST heading THEN heading EQUALS r's `heading of cited provision`

GIVEN r IS AN `External cross-reference`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the external cross-reference is to another instrument` r MEANS
        `the provision is indexed` (r's `citing provision`)
    AND NOT (r's `instrument as printed` EQUALS "Acts Interpretation Act 1931")

#ASSERT count `the internal cross-references` EQUALS 91
#ASSERT count `the external cross-references` EQUALS 118
